    "title": "The Boys Season 5 release time & schedule",
    "text": "Here's when The Boys season 5 arrives! Updated: Apr 7, 2026 11:26 am WePC is reader-supported. When you buy through links on our site, we may earn an affiliate commission. Prices subject to change. Learn more After months of waiting, The Boys is finally back, and this time it’s the final chapter. Season 5 kicks off this week, tomorrow in fact, bringing Homelander’s story to an end and setting up what should be the biggest showdown the series has seen. If you’re planning to watch as soon as it drops, here’s exactly when The Boys season 5 releases, along with the full episode schedule. And, as always, remember.. Don’t be a…. What time can you watch The Boys season 5? The Boys season 5 premieres on Wednesday, April 8, 2026, on Prime Video. The launch includes a two-episode premiere, with the remaining episodes releasing weekly. Here’s when you can expect the first episodes to go live in your region: US / Canada: 12am PT / 3am ET UK: 8am BST India: 12:30pm IST Singapore: 3pm SGT Australia: 5pm AEDT New Zealand: 7pm NZDT Release times can occasionally shift slightly, but these are the expected launch windows. The Boys season 5 episode schedule Season 5 will have 8 episodes in total, with new episodes arriving weekly: Episodes 1 & 2: April 8 Episode 3: April 15 Episode 4: April 22 Episode 5: April 29 Episode 6: May 6 Episode 7: May 13 Episode 8 (finale): May 20 Season 5 has been confirmed as the final season of The Boys. This will wrap up the main story that’s been building since the show first launched. That said, the wider universe isn’t going anywhere. Spin-offs like Gen V are expected to continue expanding the story beyond the main series.",
